00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
Sparkle is a 2012 American musical film directed by
Salim Akil and produced by Stage 6 Films.

12
01:03:16,363 --> 01:03:22,363
It was released on August 17, 2012, by TriStar Pictures.

13
01:08:32,727 --> 01:08:38,727
Inspired by The Supremes, Sparkle is a remake of the 1976 film of the same title, which
centered on three singing teenage sisters who form a girl group in the late 1950s.

14
01:13:49,090 --> 01:13:55,090
The remake takes place in Detroit, Michigan, in 1968 during the Motown era.

15
01:19:05,454 --> 01:19:11,454
The film stars Jordin Sparks in her film debut, Whitney Houston, Derek Luke, Cee Lo Green,
Mike Epps, Carmen Ejogo, Tika Sumpter, Tamela Mann, and Omari Hardwick.

16
01:24:21,818 --> 01:24:27,818
Sparkle features songs from the original film written by soul musician
Curtis Mayfield as well as new compositions by R&B artist R.

17
01:29:38,181 --> 01:29:44,181
This film is the debut of R&B/pop singer and American
Idol winner Jordin Sparks as an actress.

18
01:34:54,545 --> 01:35:00,545
Sparkle also marks Houston's final feature film role before her death
on February 11, 2012, three months after filming ended.

19
01:40:10,909 --> 01:40:16,909
The film is dedicated to her memory.

